  "verbalization": "Desmopressin, through its resemblance to Linaclotide and Felypressin, shares a common ancestry with Terlipressin, which binds to Avpr1b. This suggests a potential mechanism by which Desmopressin may interact with Avpr1b, possibly through a shared structural or functional profile. The evidence highlights a recurring pathway where a drug (Desmopressin) resembles another compound (Linaclotide or Felypressin), which in turn binds to Avpr1b. This implies that the interaction between Desmopressin and Avpr1b may be mediated by a structural or functional similarity to other compounds that already exhibit this binding activity. The lowest common ancestors of these compounds, such as the heterodetic cyclic peptide and antidiuretic hormone analogue, suggest a broader class of compounds that may share similar mechanisms of action. While the direct binding of Desmopressin to Avpr1b is not explicitly stated, the evidence supports a plausible mechanism through structural and functional similarity, aligning with the observed biological relationships.",
